diff --git a/MeetFlowAI.Win/docs/activation.md b/MeetFlowAI.Win/docs/activation.md
index 36ad3c3..69eabc5 100644
--- a/MeetFlowAI.Win/docs/activation.md
+++ b/MeetFlowAI.Win/docs/activation.md
@@ -2,7 +2,20 @@
 
 Activation does not require user login. A customer receives one activation key and the app binds that key to the first machine that activates it.
 
-## Firebase Setup
+## Production endpoint (MeetFlow API)
+
+The shipped `ActivationApiUrl` is `https://api.meetflowai.site/v1/ai/license`.
+The control-plane serves `POST /activate` and `POST /verify` with the same
+request/response contract as the Firebase functions and keeps using the
+Firestore `activationKeys` collection, so keys sold before the switch keep
+working.
+
+The app no longer keeps a local signing secret. On startup it reads the stored
+license and asks the server to `verify` the `key` + `machineId` pair; a
+hand-written `license.json` therefore cannot unlock the app. `/verify` is the
+authority for revoked keys, device limits, and expiry.
+
+## Firebase Setup (alternative backend)
 
 1. Create a Firebase project.
 2. Enable Firestore.
